{"title":"Omer Amiad's Blog","url":"https://omeramiad.com/posts/","favicon":"https://omeramiad.com/favicon-96x96.png","elements":[{"title":"Kicking the Bucket: Critical RCE and Cross-Tenant Exploits in 3 Different GCP Products","contents":"<a href=\"https://focalsecurity.io/blog/kicking-the-bucket-gcp-cross-tenant/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" class=\"inline-block text-lg font-medium text-accent decoration-dashed underline-offset-4 focus-visible:no-underline focus-visible:underline-offset-0\"> <h2 style=\"view-transition-name:kicking-the-bucket-critical-rce-and-cross-tenant-exploits-in-3-different-gcp-products\" class=\"text-lg font-medium decoration-dashed hover:underline\">Kicking the Bucket: Critical RCE and Cross-Tenant Exploits in 3 Different GCP Products</h2> </a> <div class=\"flex items-center gap-x-2 opacity-80\"> <svg width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"inline-block size-6 min-w-[1.375rem] scale-90\"><path stroke=\"none\" d=\"M0 0h24v24H0z\" fill=\"none\"></path><path d=\"M4 7a2 2 0 0 1 2 -2h12a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v12a2 2 0 0 1 -2 2h-12a2 2 0 0 1 -2 -2v-12z\"></path><path d=\"M16 3v4\"></path><path d=\"M8 3v4\"></path><path d=\"M4 11h16\"></path><path d=\"M7 14h.013\"></path><path d=\"M10.01 14h.005\"></path><path d=\"M13.01 14h.005\"></path><path d=\"M16.015 14h.005\"></path><path d=\"M13.015 17h.005\"></path><path d=\"M7.01 17h.005\"></path><path d=\"M10.01 17h.005\"></path></svg>  <time class=\"text-sm\" datetime=\"2026-04-14T15:20:35.000Z\">14 Apr, 2026</time> </div> <p>How my bucket-squatting research uncovered three cross-tenant vulnerabilities - GeminiSquat (CVE-2026-1727), MountSquat and VertexSquat (CVE-2026-2473) - affecting Gemini Enterprise, Cloud Run, and Vertex AI.\n</p>","link":"https://focalsecurity.io/blog/kicking-the-bucket-gcp-cross-tenant/","retrieved":1776180035000},{"title":"GatewayToHeaven: Finding a Critical Cross-Tenant Exploit in GCP's Apigee","contents":"<a href=\"/posts/gatewaytoheaven-gcp-cross-tenant-vulnerability\" class=\"inline-block text-lg font-medium text-accent decoration-dashed underline-offset-4 focus-visible:no-underline focus-visible:underline-offset-0\"> <h2 style=\"view-transition-name:gateway-to-heaven-finding-a-critical-cross-tenant-exploit-in-gc-ps-apigee\" class=\"text-lg font-medium decoration-dashed hover:underline\">GatewayToHeaven: Finding a Critical Cross-Tenant Exploit in GCP's Apigee</h2> </a> <div class=\"flex items-center gap-x-2 opacity-80\"> <svg width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"inline-block size-6 min-w-[1.375rem] scale-90\"><path stroke=\"none\" d=\"M0 0h24v24H0z\" fill=\"none\"></path><path d=\"M4 7a2 2 0 0 1 2 -2h12a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v12a2 2 0 0 1 -2 2h-12a2 2 0 0 1 -2 -2v-12z\"></path><path d=\"M16 3v4\"></path><path d=\"M8 3v4\"></path><path d=\"M4 11h16\"></path><path d=\"M7 14h.013\"></path><path d=\"M10.01 14h.005\"></path><path d=\"M13.01 14h.005\"></path><path d=\"M16.015 14h.005\"></path><path d=\"M13.015 17h.005\"></path><path d=\"M7.01 17h.005\"></path><path d=\"M10.01 17h.005\"></path></svg>  <time class=\"text-sm\" datetime=\"2026-01-28T08:46:35.000Z\">28 Jan, 2026</time> </div> <p>A technical step-by-step writeup about finding CVE-2025-13292, a cross-tenant vulnerability in Google Cloud's Apigee. This vulnerability allowed an attacker to gain read/write access to verbose cross-tenant access logs and analytics data that could contain access tokens of end users.</p>","link":"https://omeramiad.com/posts/gatewaytoheaven-gcp-cross-tenant-vulnerability","retrieved":1769589995000},{"title":"2Cool4School Writeup - Kalmar CTF 2023","contents":"<a href=\"/posts/2cool4school-writeup-kalmar-ctf-2023\" class=\"inline-block text-lg font-medium text-accent decoration-dashed underline-offset-4 focus-visible:no-underline focus-visible:underline-offset-0\"> <h2 style=\"view-transition-name:2-cool-4-school-writeup-kalmar-ctf-2023\" class=\"text-lg font-medium decoration-dashed hover:underline\">2Cool4School Writeup - Kalmar CTF 2023</h2> </a> <div class=\"flex items-center gap-x-2 opacity-80\"> <svg width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"inline-block size-6 min-w-[1.375rem] scale-90\"><path stroke=\"none\" d=\"M0 0h24v24H0z\" fill=\"none\"></path><path d=\"M4 7a2 2 0 0 1 2 -2h12a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v12a2 2 0 0 1 -2 2h-12a2 2 0 0 1 -2 -2v-12z\"></path><path d=\"M16 3v4\"></path><path d=\"M8 3v4\"></path><path d=\"M4 11h16\"></path><path d=\"M7 14h.013\"></path><path d=\"M10.01 14h.005\"></path><path d=\"M13.01 14h.005\"></path><path d=\"M16.015 14h.005\"></path><path d=\"M13.015 17h.005\"></path><path d=\"M7.01 17h.005\"></path><path d=\"M10.01 17h.005\"></path></svg>  <time class=\"text-sm\" datetime=\"2023-06-18T15:20:35.000Z\">18 Jun, 2023</time> </div> <p>A writeup for the web challenge 2Cool4School from Kalmar CTF 2023. This writeup examines hidden APIs discovered through Swagger documentation, finding a CSRF in the profile picture upload functionality of a website, and taking advantage of an HTTP parameter injection in a faulty SSO flow.</p>","link":"https://omeramiad.com/posts/2cool4school-writeup-kalmar-ctf-2023","retrieved":1687101635000},{"title":"ZeroTrust Writeup - LA CTF 2023","contents":"<a href=\"/posts/zerotrust-writeup-la-ctf-2023\" class=\"inline-block text-lg font-medium text-accent decoration-dashed underline-offset-4 focus-visible:no-underline focus-visible:underline-offset-0\"> <h2 style=\"view-transition-name:zero-trust-writeup-la-ctf-2023\" class=\"text-lg font-medium decoration-dashed hover:underline\">ZeroTrust Writeup - LA CTF 2023</h2> </a> <div class=\"flex items-center gap-x-2 opacity-80\"> <svg width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"inline-block size-6 min-w-[1.375rem] scale-90\"><path stroke=\"none\" d=\"M0 0h24v24H0z\" fill=\"none\"></path><path d=\"M4 7a2 2 0 0 1 2 -2h12a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v12a2 2 0 0 1 -2 2h-12a2 2 0 0 1 -2 -2v-12z\"></path><path d=\"M16 3v4\"></path><path d=\"M8 3v4\"></path><path d=\"M4 11h16\"></path><path d=\"M7 14h.013\"></path><path d=\"M10.01 14h.005\"></path><path d=\"M13.01 14h.005\"></path><path d=\"M16.015 14h.005\"></path><path d=\"M13.015 17h.005\"></path><path d=\"M7.01 17h.005\"></path><path d=\"M10.01 17h.005\"></path></svg>  <time class=\"text-sm\" datetime=\"2023-02-15T16:46:34.000Z\">15 Feb, 2023</time> </div> <p>A writeup for the web challenge ZeroTrust from LA CTF 2023. This writeup details how to exploit a misconfigured AES GCM rolling cipher to modify an authentication cookie and read the contents of the flag.</p>","link":"https://omeramiad.com/posts/zerotrust-writeup-la-ctf-2023","retrieved":1676479594000}]}